setter and getter 
______________________
In Python, setter and getter methods are used to control access to private attributes of a class. 
While you can use traditional methods (get_var() / set_var()), 
the more Pythonic way is to use the @property decorator.

 Why Use Getters and Setters?
Control access to private data

Add validation logic before setting values

Encapsulation: hide internal representation
suppose var is variable 
Approach	Syntax	Access Style
(1)Traditional	set_var(), get_var()	Explicit method call
(2)Pythonic	@property, @var.setter	Use like attribu


class Student:
	def __init__(self):
		self.__name=""
		self.__rollno=0
		self.__marks = 0  # private variable
	def set_name(self,name):
		self.__name=name 
	def set_rollno(self,rollno):
		self.__rollno=rollno
	def set_marks(self, marks):
		if marks >= 0:
			self.__marks = marks
	def get_marks(self):
		return self.__marks
	def get_name(self):
		return self.__name
	def get_rollno(self):
		return self.__rollno
obj = Student()
